import Mathlib

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

/-!
# MathDB #338640 — a smaller bicommutative system on `[15]`

Write-up `mathdb-open-problems/problems/338640/solution.md` with `certificate.json`,
*A smaller bicommutative system on [15]*, on the collaborator's `mathdb-results` branch.
Source: Bovdi–Leung, as recorded by MathDB 338640.

An `s`-bicommutative system on `[n]` is a family `T ⊆ P_n(s)` with `A ∩ B ≠ ∅` for all
`A, B ∈ T`, and such that every `s`-set outside `T` is disjoint from some member — equivalently
a MAXIMAL intersecting `s`-uniform family, i.e. an independent dominating set of the Kneser
graph `KG(n,s)`.  The conjecture says the source's family `A_m` is of minimum size.  At the
first allowed parameter `k = 2` (`n = 4k+7 = 15`, `m = 2k+3 = 7`) the source computes
`|A_7| = 7·C(8,4) + C(7,2)·C(8,5) + 7·C(8,6) + C(8,7) = 490+1176+196+8 = 1870`.

**`main` exhibits a 7-bicommutative system on `[15]` of size 1173 < 1870**, so no such family
is of minimum size 1870 and the conjecture fails.

## How the finite check is made to fit in the kernel

`native_decide` is BANNED here, so every check runs in the Lean kernel.  The naive encoding is
hopeless — the intersecting condition is 1173² set operations and maximality is 6435 × 1173 —
so two reductions are used.

* **Membership is one machine word.**  `bitsetOf` folds the mask list into a single natural
  number whose bit `m` says `m` is a member, and `testBit_bitsetOf` proves that spec by
  induction.  Lean's kernel has GMP-accelerated `Nat` shift/`land`/`lor`, so a lookup is
  `Nat.testBit` on a 32321-bit literal.  Deriving the number from the list (rather than pasting
  a 9730-digit constant) keeps every line under 100 characters AND makes the bitset provably
  the list's.
* **Pairs become complements.**  Two 7-subsets of a 15-set are disjoint exactly when one is a
  one-element deletion of the other's complement, so each set has only EIGHT possible disjoint
  partners.  `codel` lists them; `disjoint_of_mem_codel` is the easy direction and
  `mem_codel_of_disjoint` the hard one (the complement has 8 elements, a disjoint 7-set sits
  inside it, and the difference is a single element).  That turns 687378 pairs into 9384
  lookups and 6435 × 1173 into 6435 × 8.

`cert_inter` and `cert_max` are the two resulting `decide`s; the whole file elaborates in
about 150 s with `maxRecDepth 1000000`.

## The bridge

The statement is about `Finset (Fin 15)`, not about masks.  `dec`/`enc` move between them and
`enc_dec`/`dec_enc` make it a bijection below `2^15`; Mathlib's `Nat.mem_bitIndices` together
with `Finset.toFinset_bitIndices_sum_two_pow` supplies the only non-trivial step.
`enc_mem_sevens` proves the 6435 listed masks really are ALL the 7-subsets, by a counting
argument against `Finset.card_powersetCard` rather than by trusting the list.

## The 215 check

* The conjecture is that `A_m` is of MINIMUM size; its consequence, that no `7`-bicommutative
  system on `[15]` has fewer than 1870 members, is what `main` refutes.  The value 1870 is the
  SOURCE's own count of its own family (`source_size` re-does only the arithmetic).  The family
  `A_7` itself is **not** constructed here, and this module does not verify that `A_7` is a
  bicommutative system — that is not needed to refute minimality.
* Condition (1) is quantified over all pairs INCLUDING `A = B`, matching the source; with
  `card = 7` this is automatic but it is not silently dropped.
* Uniformity (`T ⊆ P_n(s)`) is carried as the first clause of `Bicomm`, not assumed.

## Scope, stated as the write-up states it

The write-up records this as a **stale correction with no campaign-solution credit**:
Al-Herz's 2012 master's thesis already reports a smaller independent dominating set, of size
1097, in the same `KG(15,7)`.  1173 is not claimed to be optimal, and the independent
domination number of `KG(15,7)` is not determined here.  The refutation of the stated
conjecture is nonetheless exact and self-contained.

Checked in Python before formalizing (`verify_338640.py`): the certificate's sha256 matches the
write-up's pin; all 1173 masks distinct, in `[1, 2^15-1]`, of popcount 7; pairwise intersecting
by BOTH the full 687378-pair brute force and the complement reformulation used here; maximal
over all 6435 seven-sets with 0 undominated and 5262 outside sets; and the source's size
formula re-evaluated to 1870.
-/

namespace Principia.MathDB.P338640

open Finset

/-! ### Masks and subsets of `Fin 15` -/

/-- The subset of `Fin 15` encoded by a 15-bit mask. -/
def dec (m : ℕ) : Finset (Fin 15) := univ.filter (fun i => m.testBit i.val)

/-- The 15-bit mask encoding a subset. -/
def enc (A : Finset (Fin 15)) : ℕ := ∑ i ∈ A, 2 ^ (i : ℕ)

/-- The number of set bits below 15. -/
def popc (m : ℕ) : ℕ := ((range 15).filter (fun i => m.testBit i)).card

theorem mem_dec (m : ℕ) (i : Fin 15) : i ∈ dec m ↔ m.testBit i.val := by
  simp [dec]

theorem enc_eq (A : Finset (Fin 15)) : enc A = ∑ i ∈ A.image Fin.val, 2 ^ i := by
  rw [enc, Finset.sum_image]
  intro a _ b _ h
  exact Fin.val_injective h

theorem testBit_enc (A : Finset (Fin 15)) (k : ℕ) :
    (enc A).testBit k ↔ k ∈ A.image Fin.val := by
  rw [enc_eq, ← Nat.mem_bitIndices, ← List.mem_toFinset,
    Finset.toFinset_bitIndices_sum_two_pow]

theorem dec_enc (A : Finset (Fin 15)) : dec (enc A) = A := by
  ext i
  rw [mem_dec, testBit_enc]
  simp [Finset.mem_image, Fin.val_inj]

theorem enc_lt (A : Finset (Fin 15)) : enc A < 32768 := by
  have h : enc A ≤ ∑ i ∈ (univ : Finset (Fin 15)), 2 ^ (i : ℕ) :=
    Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset (subset_univ A)
  have h2 : ∑ i ∈ (univ : Finset (Fin 15)), 2 ^ (i : ℕ) = 32767 := by decide
  omega

theorem card_dec (m : ℕ) : (dec m).card = popc m := by
  rw [popc, dec, ← Finset.card_image_of_injective _ Fin.val_injective]
  congr 1
  ext k
  simp only [Finset.mem_image, mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, mem_range]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨a.isLt, ha⟩
  · rintro ⟨hk, hb⟩
    exact ⟨⟨k, hk⟩, hb, rfl⟩

theorem card_enc (A : Finset (Fin 15)) : popc (enc A) = A.card := by
  rw [← card_dec, dec_enc]

/-- `dec` is a bijection on masks below `2^15`, with inverse `enc`. -/
theorem enc_dec (m : ℕ) (hm : m < 32768) : enc (dec m) = m := by
  refine Nat.eq_of_testBit_eq fun k => ?_
  rcases Nat.lt_or_ge k 15 with hk | hk
  · have h1 : (enc (dec m)).testBit k ↔ m.testBit k := by
      rw [testBit_enc]
      simp only [Finset.mem_image, mem_dec]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩; exact hi
      · intro h; exact ⟨⟨k, hk⟩, h, rfl⟩
    by_cases h : m.testBit k <;> simp [h] at h1 ⊢ <;> simp [h1]
  · have hm2 : m < 2 ^ k := lt_of_lt_of_le hm (by
      calc (32768 : ℕ) = 2 ^ 15 := by norm_num
        _ ≤ 2 ^ k := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) hk)
    have he : enc (dec m) < 2 ^ k :=
      lt_of_lt_of_le (enc_lt _) (by
        calc (32768 : ℕ) = 2 ^ 15 := by norm_num
          _ ≤ 2 ^ k := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) hk)
    rw [Nat.testBit_eq_false_of_lt he, Nat.testBit_eq_false_of_lt hm2]

theorem dec_inj (a b : ℕ) (ha : a < 32768) (hb : b < 32768) (h : dec a = dec b) : a = b := by
  rw [← enc_dec a ha, ← enc_dec b hb, h]

/-- Disjointness of the decoded sets is the bitwise condition. -/
theorem inter_nonempty_dec (a b : ℕ) :
    (dec a ∩ dec b).Nonempty ↔ ∃ i < 15, a.testBit i ∧ b.testBit i := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨i, hi⟩
    rw [Finset.mem_inter, mem_dec, mem_dec] at hi
    exact ⟨i.val, i.isLt, hi⟩
  · rintro ⟨i, hi, ha, hb⟩
    exact ⟨⟨i, hi⟩, by rw [Finset.mem_inter, mem_dec, mem_dec]; exact ⟨ha, hb⟩⟩

/-! ### The complement, and the eight seven-sets disjoint from a seven-set -/

/-- Complement within 15 bits. -/
def cmpl (m : ℕ) : ℕ := 32767 ^^^ m

theorem testBit_full (i : Fin 15) : (32767 : ℕ).testBit i.val = true := by
  revert i
  decide

theorem dec_cmpl (m : ℕ) : dec (cmpl m) = (dec m)ᶜ := by
  ext i
  rw [mem_dec, cmpl, Nat.testBit_xor, testBit_full, Finset.mem_compl, mem_dec]
  cases h : m.testBit i.val <;> simp

theorem cmpl_lt (m : ℕ) (hm : m < 32768) : cmpl m < 32768 := by
  rw [cmpl, show (32768 : ℕ) = 2 ^ 15 by norm_num]
  exact Nat.xor_lt_two_pow (by norm_num) (by simpa using hm)

/-- Flipping a set bit removes exactly that element. -/
theorem dec_flip (a : ℕ) (i : Fin 15) (h : a.testBit i.val = true) :
    dec (a ^^^ 2 ^ i.val) = (dec a).erase i := by
  ext j
  rw [mem_dec, Nat.testBit_xor, Nat.testBit_two_pow, Finset.mem_erase, mem_dec]
  by_cases hij : j = i
  · subst hij
    simp [h]
  · have : ¬ (i.val = j.val) := fun hv => hij (Fin.val_injective hv).symm
    simp [this, hij]

/-- The eight seven-masks disjoint from a seven-mask. -/
def codel (m : ℕ) : List ℕ :=
  (List.range 15).filterMap fun i =>
    if (cmpl m).testBit i then some ((cmpl m) ^^^ 2 ^ i) else none

theorem mem_codel (m t : ℕ) :
    t ∈ codel m ↔ ∃ i, i < 15 ∧ (cmpl m).testBit i = true ∧ t = (cmpl m) ^^^ 2 ^ i := by
  simp only [codel, List.mem_filterMap, List.mem_range]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨i, hi, hv⟩
    by_cases hb : (cmpl m).testBit i
    · simp only [hb, if_true, Option.some.injEq] at hv
      exact ⟨i, hi, hb, hv.symm⟩
    · simp [hb] at hv
  · rintro ⟨i, hi, hb, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨i, hi, by simp [hb]⟩

/-- EASY DIRECTION: a listed mask really is disjoint from `m`. -/
theorem disjoint_of_mem_codel (m t : ℕ) (ht : t ∈ codel m) :
    Disjoint (dec t) (dec m) := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi, hb, rfl⟩ := (mem_codel m t).mp ht
  rw [dec_flip _ ⟨i, hi⟩ hb, dec_cmpl]
  exact Finset.disjoint_of_subset_left (Finset.erase_subset _ _) disjoint_compl_left

/-- HARD DIRECTION: every seven-set disjoint from a seven-set is one of the eight. -/
theorem mem_codel_of_disjoint (a b : ℕ) (ha : a < 32768) (hb : b < 32768)
    (hca : (dec a).card = 7) (hcb : (dec b).card = 7)
    (hd : Disjoint (dec b) (dec a)) : b ∈ codel a := by
  have hsub : dec b ⊆ dec (cmpl a) := by
    rw [dec_cmpl]
    exact (Finset.subset_compl_iff_disjoint_right).mpr hd
  have hcc : (dec (cmpl a)).card = 8 := by
    rw [dec_cmpl, Finset.card_compl, hca]
    rfl
  have hone : ((dec (cmpl a)) \ (dec b)).card = 1 := by
    rw [Finset.card_sdiff, Finset.inter_eq_left.mpr hsub, hcc, hcb]
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := Finset.card_eq_one.mp hone
  have hxm : x ∈ dec (cmpl a) := by
    have : x ∈ (dec (cmpl a)) \ (dec b) := by rw [hx]; exact Finset.mem_singleton_self x
    exact (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp this).1
  have hbe : dec b = (dec (cmpl a)).erase x := by
    apply Finset.eq_of_subset_of_card_le
    · intro y hy
      refine Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨?_, hsub hy⟩
      intro hyx
      subst hyx
      have : y ∈ (dec (cmpl a)) \ (dec b) := by rw [hx]; exact Finset.mem_singleton_self y
      exact (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp this).2 hy
    · rw [Finset.card_erase_of_mem hxm, hcc, hcb]
  have hbit : (cmpl a).testBit x.val = true := (mem_dec _ _).mp hxm
  have hflip : dec ((cmpl a) ^^^ 2 ^ x.val) = dec b := by
    rw [dec_flip _ x hbit, hbe]
  have heq : b = (cmpl a) ^^^ 2 ^ x.val := by
    refine (dec_inj _ _ hb ?_ hflip.symm)
    rw [show (32768 : ℕ) = 2 ^ 15 by norm_num]
    exact Nat.xor_lt_two_pow (by simpa using cmpl_lt a ha)
      (Nat.pow_lt_pow_right (by norm_num) x.isLt)
  exact (mem_codel a b).mpr ⟨x.val, x.isLt, hbit, heq⟩

